# SABOTAGE: A2 (ADR-047 §6) gate sabotage — the operator kill-switch is checked ONCE, at
# run start (Breaker.check_start), instead of re-checked at EVERY turn boundary. An
# operator kill (or rate/provider trip throwing the same switch) landing between turn N
# and turn N+1 is silently ignored: the in-flight run keeps burning turns, budget, and
# provider spend to its own conclusion — the Automation.RunWorker "already-queued half"
# lesson (a run of a killed workflow must finalize, never fire) reversed on the agent
# path. Flips the named in-flight kill red test (a kill flipped DURING turn 2 must stop
# turn 3); the start-refusal test AND the no-kill positive control stay green — proving
# the red fails because the per-turn re-check is gone, not because the switch died.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_durability_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a kill flipped DURING turn 2 stops turn 3
